WEBVTT

00:00:00.316 --> 00:00:03.800
Ever come back hours later to check on your AI agent?

00:00:03.853 --> 00:00:07.558
It asked a question five minutes in. And it's still waiting.

00:00:07.768 --> 00:00:11.474
Meet Clawdy. It's a traffic light for your AI coding chats.

00:00:11.526 --> 00:00:16.221
Clawdy lives on your Mac or Windows PC, and there's even a little version for your desk.

00:00:16.274 --> 00:00:18.232
Amber means your chats are still working.

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:20.126
All done? Both lights go green.

00:00:20.179 --> 00:00:23.315
What if a test fails, or your AI has a question?

00:00:23.316 --> 00:00:23.579
[Clawdy squeaks]

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:26.947
When a chat needs help, Clawdy turns red and asks you to step in.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:31.053
Click Open chat, and Clawdy takes you straight to the chat that paused.

00:00:31.105 --> 00:00:35.979
Want the same lights on your desk? That's Clawdy and Clawdy Pro Max. They sync over Bluetooth.

00:00:36.032 --> 00:00:39.400
Clawdy connects to Codex, Claude Code, Gemini CLI, and Cursor.

00:00:40.768 --> 00:00:43.579
Try the Mac demo from source. No toy needed.
